:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T04:08:03-07:00","id":1443724,"title":"","content":"Thunderbolt Fantasy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T16:28:35-07:00","id":1444402,"title":"","content":"I just watched New Gods: Nezha Reborn on Netflix. Adding that to the list here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T17:10:42-07:00","id":1444410,"title":"","content":"Fate Stay/Night and the small army of spin offs it has birthed like Grand Order","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T09:09:17-07:00","id":1444513,"title":"","content":"Reposting from an rpg.net post:<br /> <br /> Core Manga Inspirations:<br /> Fist of the North Star (which I like but actually don't love *so* much as a personal thing, but it is so obviously Formative Influences Canon, and Kenshiro so absolutely a Solar)<br /> Trigun<br /> Ninja Scroll<br /> Vampire Hunter D: Bloodlust<br /> Vision of Escaflowne<br /> <br /> Less Core Inspirations (in rough order of potence):<br /> Princess Mononoke, Nausicaa<br /> Cowboy Bebop, Samurai Champloo<br /> Laputa: Castle In The Sky<br /> Slayers<br /> Street Fighter II: The Animated Movie<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Pretty much the main things in an influence are some form of &quot;Wandering guy(s) with stylish character design and awesome spiritual martial arts in a fantasy world with a post-apoc/war-torn/Wild West vibe, with lots of ruins of fallen civilization, where injustice and gritty violence are common&quot;. That's kind of &quot;The Solars&quot; after all, and &quot;The Solars&quot; is Exalted's heart. With a dash of JRPG style &quot;Heroes of Light&quot; chosen of the crystals / spirits / &quot;the planet&quot;.<br /> <br /> The less core inspirations have a similar gritty mileau but are more focused on &quot;ordinary people&quot; (though still 'heroic' and able to do some beyond real human stylish action but not supernatural, like Spike or Nausicaa), or supernatural people in a world that's either more &quot;ordinary fantasy&quot; or &quot;ordinary modern&quot; world (like Slayers, SFII). Mostly pulp adventure stories; dynastic and ruling stuff is not so tightly in focus.<br /> <br /> Common traits are where character designs are often the focus and is are detailed and exaggerated; oversized weapons, huge and stylized attacks, strong silhouettes with exaggerated proportions, lots of detail in character design and detail in character design (possibly with too many belts and scars and such!) is more important than fluidity in animation. There's probably not *too* much animation either and it's more like a literal translation of a manga into animation (as in, you can see what the panels would be, rather that the shots are using the medium to do things that wouldn't translate well to a series of static panels).<br /> <br /> All fairly old; if there's newer stuff that meets the same sort of criterion, then that's workable, I just don't know about it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T11:53:21-07:00","id":1444528,"title":"","content":"Not finding another topic for it so I'll ask here : Anyone got suggestions for &quot;Spring and Autumn China&quot; media that I could watch ? I've been using Worlds Without Numbers framework to create an Exalted setting around Brightwork in the North-West, and I rolled this period for the social reference of the local Azure Lords nation, but I don't know anything about it so I'd like to cultivate myself","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}